  "narrative": "Synthesis update at iteration 20. No validation response deadline was pending and the independent validation budget is exhausted, so no new validation request was possible. I therefore synthesized the current evidence rather than adding validation. The operational clinical rule is a 10% absolute-scale difference on the outcome magnitude. Because most CRISPR scores have negative means and more negative values mean stronger dependency, I used roughly 0.1 x absolute mean as the signed positive contrast threshold: outcome_014 about +0.0093, outcome_001 about +0.0415 under the registered negative-direction stronger-dependency claims, outcome_013 about +0.0269, outcome_006 about +0.0175, outcome_011 about +0.0301, and outcome_008 about +0.0282. Returned intervals are already signed to the registered directions.\n\nSupported findings. H14 remains robust: feature_027=1 versus 0 on outcome_014 gives signed +0.796 (R14, 95% +0.776 to +0.816) and independent validation +0.802 (R26, +0.775 to +0.829). The effect is far above the small outcome_014 threshold. Because outcome_014 is negative and direction is +1, the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is positive, so feature_027=1 is associated with a less negative outcome_014 score, i.e. weaker dependency, in this dataset. H88 is also robust: feature_050=1 versus 0 on outcome_001, registered with direction -1, gives signed +0.784 (R56, +0.765 to +0.803) and validation +0.805 (R76, +0.774 to +0.836). The signed positive estimate corresponds to a raw negative exposed-minus-comparator contrast, so feature_050=1 is associated with a more negative outcome_001 score, i.e. stronger dependency, in this dataset. Many accepted subgroup and stratified contrasts for these two predictor-outcome pairs are best read as scope/consistency checks, not many independent discoveries, because prevalence and correlated labels create near-duplicate strata. The interaction battery also mostly argues against clinically important modification of these central effects; accepted strata are stable rather than evidence of new distinct clinical subgroups.\n\nProvisional low-feature_056 candidate. The remaining concrete candidate is a low observed feature_056 feature_027 effect on outcome_013 and possibly outcome_006. H272/R240 estimates +0.075 with interval +0.027 to +0.123, nominally above the +0.0269 outcome_013 threshold but only very narrowly; the exposed n is 78, the result was subgroup-selected, and there is no validation budget. The outcome_006 low-stratum direct contrast H270/R239 gives +0.097 but interval about -0.0005 to +0.195, so it crosses both null and the +0.0175 threshold. The interaction checks H274/R241 for outcome_013 and H275/R242 for outcome_006 are imprecise and lower bounds are below their clinical thresholds. The high-feature_056 complements H273/R243 and H271/R244 are also imprecise. Therefore H272 is retained as an unresolved, active, dataset-specific candidate rather than accepted; H270, H274, and H275 remain unresolved active. This means the low-feature_056 feature_027 line is not established as clinically meaningful or as an effect-modifying subgroup.\n\nNegative and unsupported lines. Most direct predictor screens were near null or had upper bounds below clinically meaningful thresholds. Several initially promising discovery-only signals failed independent validation or were inconsistent across strata. H8 (outcome_006-feature_027) discovery +0.030 but validation R13 +0.010 near null. H13 (outcome_013-feature_027 overall) discovery +0.027 but validation R39 -0.010. H17 (outcome_003-feature_050) failed after R77. H65/H127 outcome_014-feature_042 after R102. H103 outcome_001-feature_065 after R103. H141 outcome_014-feature_065 within feature_027=0 after R116. H139 outcome_014 feature_054 interaction after R129. H227 outcome_014-feature_063 level_002 versus level_001 remains only unresolved closed: discovery R190 was above threshold, validation R192 is directionally positive but includes null and threshold. H117 was imprecise in both discovery and validation and remains unresolved closed. These rejections mean no evidence supports a clinically meaningful registered association in this dataset, not proof of exact zero.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. Remaining unresolved candidates include H285 outcome_014-feature_050 in high feature_056, H208/H240/H241/H242 borderline interactions, residual nominal level contrasts H227/H258/H259/H266/H267, rare or imprecise feature_048 contrasts H252/H253/H264/H265, feature_019 screens H268/H269, and active central-outcome interaction scope checks H215-H218/H262-H263. H253 is especially fragile because it has only 25 exposed observations despite a large point estimate. None should be promoted without stronger precision or pre-specified replication.\n\nNext analysis. The most informative discovery-only follow-up is the registered middle-feature_056 block H288-H290 plus the two new feature_050=0 low-feature_056 refinements proposed here. If the low-feature_056 feature_027 effect on outcome_013 and outcome_006 persists in the middle stratum and when feature_050=0 is fixed, it remains a plausible stratum-specific association. If it collapses or changes sign, imprecision, multiplicity, or correlated-predictor confounding is more likely. Accept only when a signed 95% lower bound clearly exceeds the relevant 10% threshold and the comparison is not rare-cell dominated; reject when the upper bound excludes the threshold; otherwise leave unresolved. All claims are associations in the supplied dataset under registered comparisons. They do not establish causality, mechanism, or external generalizability, especially because predictor labels are opaque and validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 final synthesis. Robust dataset-specific: H14 outcome_014-feature_027 (less negative score/weak dependency); H88 outcome_001-feature_050 (more negative score/strong dependency), both validated. Provisional unresolved active: low-feature_056 feature_027 effects on outcome_013/outcome_006 (H270, H272, H274, H275; complements H271, H273). Next analyze H288-H290 middle feature_056 and proposed low-feature_056 feature_050=0 refinements. Many lines failed validation or rejected; H227/H117 imprecise. No validation budget. All associations only, not causal or generalizable."
