  "narrative": "No claim assessments are due and independent validation budget is exhausted, so this explore step registers discovery-only refinements. The two robust dataset-specific associations are H14 (feature_027=1 is associated with a far less negative outcome_014 score) and H88 (feature_050=1 is associated with a far more negative outcome_001 score). I do not add many additional central consistency strata because those are already extensively supported. The remaining concrete uncertainty is whether the provisional low-feature_056 feature_027 signal is specific to low observed feature_056 on outcome_013 and possibly outcome_006, whether it is confounded by feature_050, and whether the related feature_050 contrast in low feature_056 is independent of the large feature_027 effect.\n\nFor the feature_027 claims with direction +1, a positive signed estimate means a less negative dependency score, i.e. weaker dependency. For feature_050 claims with direction -1, a positive signed estimate means a more negative dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency. I use the same operational 10% of absolute-mean thresholds as before: approximately +0.0269 for outcome_013 and +0.0175 for outcome_006 for registered positive feature_027 contrasts; for feature_050 direction -1 claims, the same signed thresholds correspond to stronger dependency if positive. Nonlow feature_056 eligibility uses feature_056 >= 40.001, while low-feature_056 eligibility uses <= 40.0; observed values partition the nonmissing feature_056 population. Missing feature_056 values are excluded, so statements are limited to observed strata.\n\nThe new comparisons test: (1) direct feature_027 contrasts in nonlow feature_056 for outcome_013 and outcome_006; (2) direct feature_027 contrasts in nonlow feature_056 restricted to feature_050=0, giving a feature_050-complement control within the same binary level; (3) interactions comparing low-feature_056 feature_027 effects against nonlow feature_027 effects while restricting to feature_050=0; and (4) feature_050 contrasts in low feature_056 restricted to feature_027=0, to test whether any low-feature_056 feature_050 signal is independent of the very large feature_027 effect. A low-specific candidate gains support if direct nonlow contrasts are below threshold or null while the feature_050-restricted low-versus-nonlow interaction has a lower bound above threshold. A broader feature_027 effect is supported if nonlow contrasts are clearly above threshold. If these comparisons remain imprecise or cross threshold, the candidate remains unresolved rather than accepted. All conclusions remain in-dataset associations among observed nonmissing strata and do not establish causality, mechanism, or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current plan: validation budget exhausted; discovery-only. Accepted central dataset-specific associations: H14 feature_027=1 -> much less negative outcome_014 (validated by R14/R26) and H88 feature_050=1 -> much more negative outcome_001 (validated by R56/R76). These are robust in this dataset but not causal/generalizable. Stratified accepted contrasts for these pairs mostly confirm scope, not independent new biology.\n\nOperational clinical thresholds: outcome_014 ~ +0.0093; outcome_001 ~ +0.0415 under feature_050 negative-direction stronger-dependency claim; outcome_013 ~ +0.0269; outcome_006 ~ +0.0175. Direction signs: feature_027 +1 positive = weaker dependency; feature_050 -1 positive signed = stronger dependency.\n\nResidual candidate: low observed feature_056 feature_027 on outcome_013. H272/R240 positive but exposed n=78 and no validation; H291/R256 restricted to feature_050=0 is positive but lower bound below threshold. Outcome_006 analogues are positive but imprecise. Middle feature_056 H288/H289 are noninformative/near null, and outcome_013 interaction H295 rejects broad positive interaction. Need to test low-specificity more cleanly and test feature_050 confounding.\n\nNew proposals: nonlow feature_056 direct feature_027 on outcome_013/006; direct nonlow feature_056 restricted to feature_050=0; low-vs-nonlow interaction restricted to feature_050=0 for outcome_013/006; feature_050 effect in low feature_056 restricted to feature_027=0 on outcome_013/006. Interpretation: if direct nonlow or restricted nonlow positive is accepted, low-specific hypothesis fails; if nonlow is rejected/low interaction accepted, low-specific candidate gains support. Feature_050 low feature_027=0 tests independence from feature_027. Do not promote unresolved low-feature_056 signals unless signed lower bounds clearly exceed thresholds. Deprioritize feature_050 on outcome_014 and rare-cell screens unless analysis reveals strong, precise effects."
