  "narrative": "Returned estimates are signed to the registered hypotheses, so a positive signed estimate supports the registered direction. I used the same operational 10% absolute-mean thresholds as earlier appraisals because the CRISPR dependency scores are negative-valued: approximately 0.0269 for outcome_013, 0.0175 for outcome_006, 0.0415 for outcome_001, 0.0093 for outcome_014, and 0.0301 for outcome_011. These are dataset-specific, observational thresholds and should not be read as causal or generalizable effect sizes.\n\nThe upper-mid observed feature_056 band tests do not provide strong evidence that the provisional feature_027 signal is broad across the observed feature_056 range. For outcome_013 in feature_056 53.0-68.999, H329 is near null and opposite to the registered positive direction, estimate -0.0019 with interval -0.053 to +0.049. Strictly, the upper confidence bound still exceeds the 0.0269 operational threshold, so I cannot reject the clinically meaningful positive hypothesis, but there is no support for acceptance and I closed this upper-mid feature_027 line as hypothesis-poor. The feature_050-restricted variant H331 is similarly unsupported, estimate -0.012 with interval -0.063 to +0.039; the upper bound is just above threshold, so it remains unresolved but closed. H330 tests direct feature_050 in the same upper-mid band for outcome_013: +0.034, interval -0.038 to +0.106. The point is suggestive of a clinically meaningful stronger-dependency association, but the interval crosses null and threshold, so it is unresolved and closed as too imprecise. The corresponding outcome_006 upper-mid tests are also imprecise: H332 feature_027 is +0.079, interval -0.017 to +0.176, and H333 feature_050 is +0.041, interval -0.083 to +0.165. Both intervals are too wide to accept and too broad to reject, so they remain unresolved closed.\n\nH334 is the most decisive new negative result. In lower-half observed feature_056, feature_027 for outcome_001 gives a signed estimate -0.040, interval -0.104 to +0.0239. The upper bound is below the 0.0415 operational threshold for outcome_001, so a clinically meaningful positive feature_027 effect on outcome_001 is rejected. This argues against a broad low-feature_056 feature_027 signal across all dependency scores and helps keep the unresolved active line outcome_013-specific, though it does not prove that no negative or small effect exists on outcome_001.\n\nThe feature_019 analyses did not establish new robust central claims. H268, direct feature_019 level_001 versus level_002 on outcome_014, is modest and imprecise: +0.011, interval -0.027 to +0.050. It cannot be accepted or rejected clinically and is closed. H269 for outcome_001 is registered as a negative signed claim but reports a signed interval entirely on the opposite side, -0.050 with CI -0.087 to -0.012. The absolute magnitude exceeds the 0.0415 threshold, so this is not a null result; rather, it is an opposite-direction association that was not the registered hypothesis. I therefore reject the registered H269 claim and close it. Because of multiplicity and lack of independent validation, the opposite feature_019 signal is only hypothesis-generating and is not accepted.\n\nThe feature_019 interaction screens also did not support clinically meaningful effect modification of the robust central contrasts. H217, interaction of feature_027 on outcome_014 within feature_019 level_002, is essentially null and imprecise: -0.0003, CI -0.041 to +0.040. Because the interval still includes clinically meaningful positive values, it is unresolved, but closed. H218, interaction of feature_050 on outcome_001 within feature_019 level_002, has upper bound +0.0237 below the 0.0415 threshold for the registered negative-signed claim, so the clinically meaningful registered positive-support interaction is rejected; the interval also includes opposite values beyond threshold, but those are unregistered and should not be accepted.\n\nThe remaining new small-cell or coverage items are low priority. H264 completes the feature_048 level_002 versus level_001 contrast for outcome_014: +0.0057 with interval -0.155 to +0.166 and exposed cell n=25; this is too unstable to interpret and remains unresolved closed. H277 tests feature_027 in the top observed feature_056 band for outcome_011: -0.038, CI -0.111 to +0.034. The upper bound exceeds the 0.0301 threshold, so the registered positive clinically meaningful hypothesis is not rejected, but there is no support for acceptance; it is closed as unresolved. Overall, none of the new due results justifies accepting a new clinically meaningful claim. The central supported dataset-specific claims remain H14 and H88. The most informative unresolved line remains low observed feature_056 feature_027 on outcome_013, where upper-mid nullity supports but does not prove localization to lower observed bands. No validation request is possible because the independent validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis update after appraise iteration 25. Validation request budget is exhausted and no new response deadline is open. Supported central dataset-specific claims remain H14 outcome_014 feature_027 (R14 and validation R26), interpreted as feature_027=1 having much weaker dependency, and H88 outcome_001 feature_050 (R56 and validation R76), interpreted as feature_050=1 having much stronger dependency. Accepted subgroup versions of these two contrasts remain robustness checks, not separate mechanisms.\n\nNew appraise results: upper-mid observed feature_056 band tests H329/H331 for outcome_013 feature_027 are null/opposite and closed; H330/H333 direct feature_050 tests are wide and closed; outcome_006 upper-mid H332/H333 are suggestive but imprecise and closed. H334 rejects a clinically meaningful positive lower-half feature_056 feature_027 association for outcome_001, arguing against a generic low-feature_056 feature_027 signal across all outcomes and supporting outcome-specific focus on outcome_013. H269 registered a negative-signed outcome_001 feature_019 contrast but evidence is opposite and clinically meaningful by absolute mean threshold; reject registered H269 and treat the opposite feature_019 signal as unregistered, hypothesis-generating only. H268 outcome_014 feature_019 is unresolved closed due imprecision. H217 outcome_014 feature_027 interaction by feature_019 level_002 is unresolved closed; H218 outcome_001 feature_050 interaction by feature_019 level_002 is rejected for registered positive support and closed. H264 feature_048 level_002 versus level_001 outcome_014 remains too small-cell and imprecise. H277 top-band outcome_011 feature_027 remains unresolved closed.\n\nThe main active uncertainty remains low observed feature_056 feature_027 on outcome_013. Existing positive estimates in feature_056 <= 40, <= 52, and feature_056 <= 40 with feature_050=0 are suggestive but not precise enough for a clean 10% clinical subgroup claim. The null upper-mid band and rejected outcome_001 lower-half pattern make a lower-band, outcome-specific interpretation more plausible but do not establish it. Outcome_006 remains weaker and inconsistent. H299 and H265 remain low-priority unresolved items from earlier. Because all conclusions are observational, feature_056 eligibility excludes missing rows, and the number of comparisons is large, no causal or generalizable claim is warranted. A future adequately powered, prespecified external replication of low-feature_056 feature_027 versus feature_050/missingness-stratified outcome_013 contrasts would be the most informative next step."
