eature_056. These rejections indicate that the registered positive or clinically meaningful hypotheses are not supported in this dataset; they are not proof of exact null effects or of absence in all populations. The main unresolved uncertainty is the low observed feature_056 feature_027 association on outcome_013. Evidence in feature_056 <=40, feature_056 <=52, and feature_056 <=40 with feature_050=0 points in the same direction, but precision is insufficient for a clean clinically meaningful subgroup claim; H272/R240, H310/R277, H291/R256, and H322/R289 are suggestive but borderline. Upper-mid band H329/R301 and H331/R303 are null or opposite, supporting but not proving localization to lower observed feature_056. Outcome_006 evidence is weaker and inconsistent, and other low-priority unresolved items such as H299 feature_055 level_003 versus level_001 for outcome_006 and H265 feature_048 level_002 versus level_001 for outcome_001 are limited by small cells and wide intervals. Overall, the supported conclusions are narrow and dataset-specific: feature_027 status is strongly associated with a much less negative outcome_014 score, and feature_050 status is strongly associated with a much more negative outcome_001 score. The most informative next analysis would be an adequately powered, prespecified external replication of low observed feature_056 feature_027 versus feature_056 higher or missing-stratified outcome_013 contrasts, with explicit feature_050 and missingness handling and a prespecified 10% clinical threshold; external replication of H14 and H88 would also be valuable for generalizability. All claims remain observational associations within the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or population-wide generalizability.",
